{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":183,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","line":489,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[homogeneity of a geodesic]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-2-6}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.6}\n  If the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,v)$ is defined on $(-\\delta,\\delta)$, then for\n  $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$, $a>0$, the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,av)$ is defined on\n  $(-\\frac{\\delta}{a},\\frac{\\delta}{a})$ and\n\n  $$\n  \\gamma(t,q,av)=\\gamma(at,q,v).\n  $$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  Let $h:(-\\frac{\\delta}{a},\\frac{\\delta}{a})\\to M$, $h(t)=\\gamma(at,q,v)$.\n  Then $h(0)=q$, $\\frac{dh}{dt}(0)=av$, and by \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n  $h$ is a geodesic (with $h'(t)=a\\gamma'(at,q,v)$), so\n\n  $$\n  \\frac{D}{dt}\\Big(\\frac{dh}{dt}\\Big)=\\nabla_{h'(t)}h'(t)=a^2\\nabla_{\\gamma'(at,q,v)}\\gamma'(at,q,v)=0.\n  $$\n\n  So $h$ is a geodesic through $q$ with velocity $av$ at $t=0$; by uniqueness\n  $h(t)=\\gamma(at,q,v)=\\gamma(t,q,av)$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[homogeneity of a geodesic] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d322d36\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-6-reparam\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-5-unique\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:2.6</span></span>If the geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t,q,v)$\">$\\gamma (t,q,v)$</span> is defined on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-\\delta ,\\delta )$\">$(-\\delta ,\\delta )$</span>, then for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a\\in \\mathbb {R}$\">$a\\in \\mathbb {R}$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a&gt;0$\">$a&gt;0$</span>, the geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t,q,av)$\">$\\gamma (t,q,av)$</span> is defined on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-\\frac{\\delta }{a},\\frac{\\delta }{a})$\">$(-\\frac{\\delta }{a},\\frac{\\delta }{a})$</span> and <p></p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\gamma (t,q,av)=\\gamma (at,q,v).  \\]\">\\[  \\gamma (t,q,av)=\\gamma (at,q,v).  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h:(-\\frac{\\delta }{a},\\frac{\\delta }{a})\\to M$\">$h:(-\\frac{\\delta }{a},\\frac{\\delta }{a})\\to M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h(t)=\\gamma (at,q,v)$\">$h(t)=\\gamma (at,q,v)$</span>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h(0)=q$\">$h(0)=q$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\frac{dh}{dt}(0)=av$\">$\\frac{dh}{dt}(0)=av$</span>, and by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-6-reparam\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d322d362d7265706172616d\">subsection 1.1</a> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h$\">$h$</span> is a geodesic (with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h&#x27;(t)=a\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)$\">$h&#x27;(t)=a\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)$</span>), so </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\frac{D}{dt}\\Big(\\frac{dh}{dt}\\Big)=\\nabla _{h&#x27;(t)}h&#x27;(t)=a^2\\nabla _{\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)}\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)=0.  \\]\">\\[  \\frac{D}{dt}\\Big(\\frac{dh}{dt}\\Big)=\\nabla _{h&#x27;(t)}h&#x27;(t)=a^2\\nabla _{\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)}\\gamma &#x27;(at,q,v)=0.  \\]</span></p><p>So <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h$\">$h$</span> is a geodesic through <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span> with velocity <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$av$\">$av$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t=0$\">$t=0$</span>; by uniqueness <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h(t)=\\gamma (at,q,v)=\\gamma (t,q,av)$\">$h(t)=\\gamma (at,q,v)=\\gamma (t,q,av)$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-pointwise","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-pointwise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-pointwise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-7","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#rem:dc-ch3-2-8","title":"rem:dc-ch3-2-8","label":"rem:dc-ch3-2-8"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","title":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","label":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1ball","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1ball"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c2ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c2ball","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c2ball"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-5-rayode","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-5-rayode","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-5-rayode"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[homogeneity of a geodesic]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-2-6}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.6}\n  If the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,v)$ is defined on $(-\\delta,\\delta)$, then for\n  $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$, $a>0$, the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,av)$ is defined on\n  $(-\\frac{\\delta}{a},\\frac{\\delta}{a})$ and\n\n  $$\n  \\gamma(t,q,av)=\\gamma(at,q,v).\n  $$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  Let $h:(-\\frac{\\delta}{a},\\frac{\\delta}{a})\\to M$, $h(t)=\\gamma(at,q,v)$.\n  Then $h(0)=q$, $\\frac{dh}{dt}(0)=av$, and by \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam}\n  $h$ is a geodesic (with $h'(t)=a\\gamma'(at,q,v)$), so\n\n  $$\n  \\frac{D}{dt}\\Big(\\frac{dh}{dt}\\Big)=\\nabla_{h'(t)}h'(t)=a^2\\nabla_{\\gamma'(at,q,v)}\\gamma'(at,q,v)=0.\n  $$\n\n  So $h$ is a geodesic through $q$ with velocity $av$ at $t=0$; by uniqueness\n  $h(t)=\\gamma(at,q,v)=\\gamma(t,q,av)$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6-reparam","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}